From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ORDER_PROBE read once (checker fix to 1038)

Checker fix to 1038 (waveydude's W-23 marker, author waveydude, GreenHatBoy discussion 2,
comment 19600367). 1038 called getenv on the GPU thread for every present whenever two guard
slots were set, probe or not, and captured three more values in every callback. Now the switch
is read once into a static; unset, the exact T181 callback is queued (no getenv, same capture),
so off is T181. Set, his callback runs as he wrote it minus the per-call getenv; the log text
and counting are unchanged. Touches nx2_gsv.h only: KEEPS THE STORE.
---
diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
--- a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
+++ b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
@@ -2220,10 +2220,15 @@
                 // EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ORDER_PROBE=1 (waveydude's W-23 marker, off unless set):
                 // logs when this marker runs while a channel is suspended on a semaphore and
                 // this present's fence is still pending; first 16 events, then every 64th.
+                // Read once (checker): unset, T181's own callback runs, no getenv per present.
+                static const bool order_probe = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ORDER_PROBE");
+                if (!order_probe) {
+                    system.GPU().RunInOrder(
+                        [n = m_presents] { VideoCommon::AheadGuard::BackPassed(n); });
+                } else {
                 system.GPU().RunInOrder([sys = &system, n = m_presents, fence_id = ~w[22],
                                          fence_value = w[24]] {
-                    if (Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ORDER_PROBE") &&
-                        sys->GPU().HasSuspendedChannels() &&
+                    if (sys->GPU().HasSuspendedChannels() &&
                         !sys->Host1x().GetSyncpointManager().IsReadyGuest(fence_id, fence_value)) {
                         static std::atomic<u64> pending_markers{};
                         const u64 count = pending_markers.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
@@ -2236,6 +2241,7 @@
                     }
                     VideoCommon::AheadGuard::BackPassed(n);
                 });
+                }
             }
         }
         m_previous2_fence_id = m_previous_fence_id;
